    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0664" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/9187: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-23T16:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 23, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 23—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>151. Secret for the President. Pursuant to your authorization<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d490-f1"/> I requested General Pershing to detail such officer in
                    his command as he considered most competent to undertake the work of estimating
                    the damage done by the Germans in Belgium and northern France on account of
                    which reparation should be required from Germany. General Pershing has detailed
                    for this work Brigadier General C. H. McKinstry. I have conferred with General
                    McKinstry and have asked him to advise me after he has considered the problem
                    how he believes this work [should?] be done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
